        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description
  >Escalates a case the moment it passes its SLA Due. A scheduled path runs 0 hours after SLA_Due__c for each open, not-yet-escalated case (Salesforce reschedules it if SLA Due changes and cancels it if the case stops matching, e.g. closes). It sets Escalated = true and Priority = High, then sends the community manager a bell notification. Escalated = true takes the case out of the entry criteria, so it is never escalated twice. Chosen over a scheduled flow because scheduled flows can only run daily or weekly, not hourly.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <interviewLabel
  >Case - Escalate Overdue {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>Case - Escalate Overdue</label>
